# Terraform
**/.terraform/*
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
crash.log
crash.*.log
*.tfplan
tfplan
# Provider lockfiles belong to root configurations, which commit theirs. This
# one only appears when `terraform validate` is run inside the module directly.
terraform/wif/.terraform.lock.hcl
override.tf
override.tf.json
*_override.tf
*_override.tf.json
.terraformrc
terraform.rc

# uv resolves from pyproject.toml directly — CI runs `uv pip install -e .`,
# not `uv sync`, so the lockfile is a local artifact rather than a build input.
# The SDK is already pinned exactly in pyproject.toml.
uv.lock

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Env
.env
.venv-dev/
terraform/environments/fixture/.terraform.lock.hcl

# Fixture data names private repositories: paths, line numbers, defect claims,
# and verbatim reference-review text. This repository is public. The harness
# code is committed; the code under measurement never is. Populate a working
# set locally with evals/curate_fixture.py, or point AGY_EVAL_FIXTURES at a
# private directory.
evals/fixtures/*.json
evals/reference/
